hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16351","He said: Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, from 'Urwah ibn Abdullah ibn Qushayr al-Ju'fi, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah narrated to me, from his father, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among a group of Muzaynah, and we pledged him, and indeed his shirt was unbuttoned, so I pledged him, and I put my hand inside the opening of the shirt and touched the Seal. 'Urwah said: I never saw Mu'awiyah nor his father, in winter nor in heat, but with their buttons undone, never buttoning ever."
"16352","He said: Sulayman narrated to us: Rawh narrated to us, he said: Bistam ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, he said: My father said: We lived long with our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we had no food but the two black ones. Then he said: Do you know what the two black ones are? I said: No. He said: Dates and water."
"16353","He said: Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he had milked and curdled. He said:"
"16354","Sulayman narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Mu'awiyah, he said: My father narrated to us, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I do not know whether he heard it from him or it was narrated to him."
"16355","He said: Abd al-Malik ibn 'Amr narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Maysarah narrated to us: Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah narrated to us, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade these two foul trees, and said: Whoever eats them, let him not approach our mosque. And he said: If you must eat them, then kill them by cooking. He said: Meaning onion and garlic."
"16356","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah Abu Iyas, he said: I heard my father, and he had met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he wiped his head and sought forgiveness for him."
"16357","'Affan narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said concerning fasting three days of the month: The fast of the lifetime and its breaking."
"16358","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to me, from Abu Iyas, he said: My father came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was a small boy, so he wiped his head and sought forgiveness for him. Shu'bah said: We said to him: Companionship? He said: No, but he was in his time, he had milked and curdled."
